docs/context/decision_log.md-994-### D-60 · Secondary button without drop shadow (design system) — 2026-10-24 · **REVERTED same day**
docs/context/decision_log.md-995-- **Reverted (Apurva, 2026-10-24):** keep the secondary button as SALT has it today — white, grey border, brand label, drop shadow. The change below was undone; recorded so it isn't proposed again without new information.
docs/context/decision_log.md-996-- **Decision (Apurva):** `.tm-btn--secondary` keeps SALT's white fill, grey border (`--tm-border-default`) and brand label, but **drops SALT's drop shadow** (`--tm-shadow-button-secondary`). Fixed centrally in `design-system/src/components.css`; listed in `beyond-salt.md`; `RULES.md` wording corrected (it said "brand border", which never matched SALT or the code).
docs/context/decision_log.md-997-- **Why:** SALT gives only the secondary a shadow and the primary none, so secondaries looked raised above the main action. The doctor app is the design system's first project; a clear miss is fixed at the source.
docs/context/decision_log.md-998-- **Rejected:** keeping the shadow for parity with SALT; a blue border (never SALT).
docs/context/decision_log.md-999-- Render: `docs/renders/2026-10-22-calling/secondary-shadow-before-after.png`. Affects every screen with a secondary button (approved A–D renders show the old shadow until re-rendered).
