docs/renders/2026-11-09-build-fast/TERMINAL-BRIEF.md-21-
docs/renders/2026-11-09-build-fast/TERMINAL-BRIEF.md-22-- Plan v3.2 §3 "how it's built" (B1–B14): one file per screen or sheet, the core modules from steps 0–1, mock server and call simulator, one app clock, settings, `MSG()` copy, state map, phone Back, remembering.
docs/renders/2026-11-09-build-fast/TERMINAL-BRIEF.md-23-- **Lift the approved markup and classes** from `ui-screens/<journey>/…html` (and `home-reference.js`, `case.html`). One CSS file per journey, using only `--tm-*` / `.tm-*`. No inline styles. Every word through `MSG()`, adding registry keys only for labels the pictures already show. Locked flow, CTAs and the valid-call gate exactly as in `app-logic.md`. Don't invent logic: use `[OPEN DECISION]` / `[MOCK ASSUMPTION]` as in CLAUDE.md.
docs/renders/2026-11-09-build-fast/TERMINAL-BRIEF.md-24-- **"Lift" means structure, not a paste.** The reference files hold every state on one page, with a state switcher and demo scripts. Don't copy those parts. Take each screen's markup structure and class names into a screen module that renders from app state. Styles: the central design system first (`truemeds.css`, `.tm-*`), then one small CSS file per journey for what is specific to it. Words go in `messages.json` (`MSG()`), mock data in `app/data/`, rules in the core modules.
docs/renders/2026-11-09-build-fast/TERMINAL-BRIEF.md-25-- **Build shared pieces once and reuse them:** case header, pinned action bar with its notice band, bottom-sheet template, medicine row, notices, toasts, confirm buttons. A screen composes them. No CSS rule repeated across journey files: if two journeys need it, it goes in a shared file.
docs/renders/2026-11-09-build-fast/TERMINAL-BRIEF.md-26-- Existing checks keep passing: `entry-journeys.mjs`, `run-checks.mjs`, `check-sources.mjs`, `layout_check.py --app`, `check_lockup.py`, `scan.mjs`.
docs/renders/2026-11-09-build-fast/TERMINAL-BRIEF.md-27-- **Commit and push after every step** (`scripts/publish.sh`, own files only, named). "Pushed to …" is the checkpoint. Never `main`, no PR, no deploy. Wait and retry on `.lock` files (the PRD tab works in this folder too).
docs/renders/2026-11-09-build-fast/TERMINAL-BRIEF.md-28-- On this Mac: `CHROME=` / `CHROMIUM=` (installed Chrome) for tests; `< /dev/null` on `codex exec`; `git -C`, never `cd && git`.
