docs/renders/2026-11-09-build-fast/TERMINAL-BRIEF.md-32-- **No per-state pixel gate.** Run `tests/compare-step1.mjs` (extend its state list to the new steps) **once at the end of each run, as a report**: list states whose changed area is over 1% of the picture, with the side-by-side sheet. Fix those only if the cause is wrong markup, a missing element or the wrong state. Anti-aliasing, retries and region explanations are not needed.
docs/renders/2026-11-09-build-fast/TERMINAL-BRIEF.md-33-- **Tests only where the logic is real:** valid-call gate (50 s, talk time across calls, fast-forward), call outcomes → screen (one test per calling-flow edge from the state map, as B15 already asks), Confirm routing (prescription / transfer / forward / Skip HA), hold and retry, callback refused, release refused, availability ends mid-case, reopen into an open case. Screens that only display a state need no test of their own; opening from `?s=` is enough (one loop over all ids).
docs/renders/2026-11-09-build-fast/TERMINAL-BRIEF.md-34-- **Codex is the tester and the critic (see "Codex in each run" below).** Spend freely on it; don't skip or shorten its steps to save time.
docs/renders/2026-11-09-build-fast/TERMINAL-BRIEF.md-35-- No per-session screenshots or contact sheets. One sheet per run (`run-<A|B>/sheet.png`: the demo path at 390, one picture per screen).
