../../design-system/RULES.md:114:## 7. Phone-frame prototypes (layout rule — do not re-litigate)
../../design-system/RULES.md-115-
../../design-system/RULES.md-116-Mobile-first prototypes are previewed on desktop as a **phone frame at the real phone shape (390 × 844, about 19.5:9)**, never as a stretched page, a narrow column glued to the window, or a dialog layout. *(Changed 2026-11-09, Apurva, doctor portal D-97: was 9:16, which is wider and shorter than today's phones and than the approved pictures.)*
../../design-system/RULES.md-117-
../../design-system/RULES.md-118-1. **Below 768px** the app *is* the screen: the window scrolls and overlays are viewport-fixed.
../../design-system/RULES.md-119-2. **At 768px and up** the app sits in a centred phone frame at 390 : 844: `height: clamp(640px, 100vh - 48px, 844px)`, `width: height × 390/844`, so it is exactly 390 × 844 when the window allows and scales down evenly when it doesn't. Rounded border, `overflow: hidden`, `transform: translateZ(0)`.
../../design-system/RULES.md-120-3. **One scroll area** inside the frame (the content region). The header is pinned above it. The page behind never scrolls because of the frame, and no side panel may be a scroll container.
../../design-system/RULES.md-121-4. **Overlays live inside the frame.** Bottom sheets, full-screen viewers, toasts and snackbars are DOM children of the frame (the transform makes `position: fixed` anchor to it). Bottom sheets keep the mobile bottom-sheet behaviour at every width; they are never turned into centred dialogs on desktop.
../../design-system/RULES.md-122-5. **Demo/dev panels** float beside the frame (absolutely positioned), **top-aligned with the frame's top edge**, in **one column on the right** of the frame. They never change its size or centring.
../../design-system/RULES.md-123-6. Desktop overrides go in one block at the END of the stylesheet so they beat the mobile rules.
../../design-system/RULES.md-124-7. Check before every commit that touches layout: `python3 projects/<project>/docs/layout_check.py` must say ALL PASS (frame 390 : 844, panels top-aligned, wheel scroll works, sheet at frame bottom, Rx viewer fills frame, no page errors).
../../design-system/RULES.md-125-
../../design-system/RULES.md-126-## 8. Mobile screen layout  [ADDED 2026-10-14 · layout v2 · D-42–D-45]
../../design-system/RULES.md-127-
../../design-system/RULES.md-128-1. **Type scale — four levels per screen.**
../../design-system/RULES.md-129-
../../design-system/RULES.md-130-   | Level | Use | Style |
../../design-system/RULES.md-131-   |---|---|---|
../../design-system/RULES.md-132-   | L1 | Screen title | `.tm-text-title-lg` 32/40 semibold |
../../design-system/RULES.md-133-   | L2 | Key content (values, names, the thing acted on) | `.tm-text-body-lg` 16/24 (or `-strong` where emphasis matters) |
../../design-system/RULES.md-134-   | L3 | Supporting text (descriptions, helper, status lines) | `.tm-text-body-md` 14/20, `--tm-content-secondary` |
../../design-system/RULES.md-135-   | L4 | Fine print (consent, legal) | `.tm-text-body-sm` 12/16, `--tm-content-secondary` |
../../design-system/RULES.md-136-
../../design-system/RULES.md-137-   Only the screen title is large; buttons keep their design-system style. Don't introduce in-between sizes.
../../design-system/RULES.md-138-   **Small sizes:** 9–11px text tokens are never used in apps. 12px only for tags and L4 fine print. Anything the user needs to act on (clinical details, amounts, status, errors) is 14px or larger.
../../design-system/RULES.md-139-   The type scale applies to screen text. Component internals (OTP digits, button labels, keyboard) keep their component specs.
../../design-system/RULES.md-140-2. **Side margin:** `--tm-space-page` (**16**, the design team's standard — changed from 24 on 2026-10-26, D-67) on every mobile screen, including the header, sheets and the action bar. Every block — fields, notices, cards, code boxes, buttons — shares the same left and right edges.
../../design-system/RULES.md-141-3. **Three gaps only:** tight `--tm-space-sm` (8): label↔field, field↔helper, and a result notice ↔ the control it came from (A-14) · related `--tm-space-lg` (16): items within a group, **and cards stacked one above another — the same gap everywhere cards stack, on the case page, Prescribe and Profile (B-04, B-05, A-13, 2026-11-02)** · section `--tm-space-2xl` (32): between groups. Spare vertical space goes between the content and a pinned button, never inside a group.
../../design-system/RULES.md-142-   Home-base screens use 3xl (48) as the hero gap between logo and title.
../../design-system/RULES.md-143-4. **Main button placement:**
../../design-system/RULES.md-144-   - **Screens with text entry:** the primary button sits inline directly under the content, so it stays visible above the keyboard without moving.
../../design-system/RULES.md-145-   - **Screens without text entry:** the primary button is pinned to the bottom with the safe-area inset; a secondary/quiet action sits below it.
../../design-system/RULES.md-146-   - **Pinned bar (Round 4, 2026-11-02):** every pinned main action — case page, Prescribe, Home, faster sign-in offer, returning unlock — sits in `.tm-actionbar` (§3). The content above it scrolls; the bar never covers the last content at the end of the scroll (§8.14). Toasts sit above the bar.
../../design-system/RULES.md-147-5. **Header types** (each product decides which screens use which):
../../design-system/RULES.md-148-   - **Home-base header:** product logo/lockup left, icon actions right.
../../design-system/RULES.md-149-   - **Task header:** Back + screen title, no logo. **Back only where there is a previous screen** to return to; screens that open a journey (e.g. a launch screen, a post-sign-in offer) have none. Two sizes:
../../design-system/RULES.md-150-     - **Hero** — tall tinted band, title `.tm-text-title-lg` 32/40. For short step screens with little content.
../../design-system/RULES.md-151-     - **Compact** — short sticky tinted band, title `.tm-text-h1` 20/28, meta lines under it. For dense work screens. Never changes height while scrolling. When Back is hidden, the title and meta move to the left margin. Long titles wrap to at most two lines; the height is set per screen, never while scrolling.  [ENHANCED 2026-10-15]
../../design-system/RULES.md-152-   - **Edit screen header** [ADDED 2026-10-15] — for a full-screen editor opened over a page (e.g. Prescribe). White bar: ✕ on the left (closes; asks before discarding unsaved changes), title 20/28 with an optional one-line subtitle, at most one action on the right (destructive outline if it removes something). A pinned summary band may sit directly under it.
../../design-system/RULES.md-153-   - **Viewer header** [ADDED 2026-10-15] — for full-screen viewers (e.g. a prescription image). Dark bar: ✕, title, tools (zoom, rotate, fit) using `.tm-btn--on-dark`. The title never overlaps the tools; it truncates first.
../../design-system/RULES.md-154-   - **Header edge (B-07, Round 5, Apurva 2026-11-02; Round 6 reading):** in the compact task header, the edit header and the viewer header, the Back / ✕ button is a 48px target whose 20px glyph starts on the 16px page margin (the target overhangs 14px to the left; glyph centre 26px from the edge), and the title starts 54px from the edge on every header type alike. The sheet ✕ uses the same edge (§9.4).
../../design-system/RULES.md-155-6. **Tap targets:** **48px minimum** for everything tappable that is not a link inside a sentence: icon buttons (✕, ?, Back, zoom), buttons, chips, rows, toggles, standalone links. Enlarge the hit area, not the text. Meets Android (48dp) and iOS (44pt); WCAG 2.5.8's floor is 24px. Links inside a sentence follow WCAG 2.5.8's inline exception.  [CHANGED 2026-10-15, was 44]
../../design-system/RULES.md-156-7. **Contrast:** all text meets WCAG AA (4.5:1; 3:1 for 24px+ or 18.66px+ bold) on the surface it sits on, including tinted bands and notices. Blue means "tap me" (§2.5): links are always `--tm-content-brand`, never grey-and-underlined. Disabled controls are exempt from the contrast rule (WCAG 1.4.3) and keep the design-system disabled style.
../../design-system/RULES.md-157-8. **Loading primary:** brand-blue fill, white label and white spinner (`.tm-btn--busy` with `.tm-spinner`) on every screen. Never grey, pale or disabled-looking.
../../design-system/RULES.md-158-9. **Keyboard clearance:** keep at least 16px between the inline main button and an open keyboard. If the content does not fit, the content scrolls.
../../design-system/RULES.md-159-10. **Titles:** no full stop at the end of a screen title. Titles wrap balanced (L8).
../../design-system/RULES.md-160-11. **Decorative icons** (bullets, list markers) are neutral (`--tm-content-secondary`); brand blue is for actions and selection only (§2.5). An icon tile used as a screen's hero may stay brand-tinted.
../../design-system/RULES.md-161-12. **Value display:** a large status value (e.g. time remaining) is a component, not screen text: 32/40 semibold, fixed-width digits (L9). Like OTP digits, it sits outside the four-level type scale.
../../design-system/RULES.md-162-13. **Logo lockup size and place (A-07, 2026-11-02).** Every home-base screen with the "truemeds for doctors" lockup (`brand/truemeds-for-doctors.svg`, project level, §2.8) draws it **166px wide** (height follows the 220×54 artwork), **16px from the top**, and the logo→title gap stays as in §8.3 (L6). 166 is the largest width that fits Home at 360 wide with 16 to the first header icon: 360 − 2×16 − (3 × 48 + 2 × 8 − 14 for the actions' 14px overhang) − 16 = 166. Sign-in is 174 today and comes down to 166 (NEEDS-APURVA, Round 4). Nothing else sets the lockup size.
../../design-system/RULES.md-163-14. **Small phones (Round 4, 2026-11-02).** At **360 × 640** every state of a screen is checked: nothing the doctor needs is hidden without a scroll cue (a visible edge of the next item, or a scroll area), and a pinned bar never covers the last content when the content is scrolled to its end. The check runs as a permanent guard in `ui-screens/feedback/check-locked-specs.py` (small-phone pass, every state, Round 4 item 10; `docs/layout_check.py` covers the old prototype only). Prescribe, the case page, Home, the offer and the unlock must pass it before a screen is approved.
../../design-system/RULES.md-164-
../../design-system/RULES.md-165-### Locked specs (D-46, D-47) — set once in the design system, never per screen
../../design-system/RULES.md-166-
../../design-system/RULES.md-167-These are fixed. A change needs Apurva's approval and an update to D-46. `ui-screens/feedback/check-locked-specs.py` fails the build if any of them is violated.
../../design-system/RULES.md-168-
../../design-system/RULES.md-169-| ID | Spec |
../../design-system/RULES.md-170-|---|---|
../../design-system/RULES.md-171-| L1 | OTP code boxes (`.tm-otp-slots`): square 56×56 slots, 24px digits, one tight centred group, gap 8 (`--tm-space-sm`). Never stretched, never 16px digits. |
../../design-system/RULES.md-172-| L2 | Loading primary buttons: brand-blue fill, white label, white spinner, on every screen (sign-in "Sending OTP", OTP "Verifying", any future loading primary). |
../../design-system/RULES.md-173-| L3 | OTP keyboard stays open during "Verifying" (D-44). Only locked and expired-and-resend-limited close it. |
../../design-system/RULES.md-174-| L4 | Field helper and field error text: 14/20 (`.tm-field__helper`). |
../../design-system/RULES.md-175-| L5 | Notice text (`.tm-notice`): 14/20. |
../../design-system/RULES.md-176-| L6 | Sign-in logo-to-title gap: 48 (`--tm-space-3xl`), home-base hero gap. |
../../design-system/RULES.md-177-| L7 | Field helper/error text aligns with its field: left under full-width fields, centred under the centred OTP code boxes (D-47). |
../../design-system/RULES.md-178-| L8 | Screen titles wrap balanced — never a single word alone on the last line (D-47). |
../../design-system/RULES.md-179-| L9 | Value display (e.g. Home time remaining): 32/40 semibold, fixed-width digits (D-47). |
../../design-system/RULES.md-180-
../../design-system/RULES.md-181-## 9. Components and states  [ADDED 2026-10-15 · design-system review · checked against Material 3, Apple HIG, WCAG 2.2]
../../design-system/RULES.md-182-
../../design-system/RULES.md-183-Set once in the design system; a project never restyles them. Where `src/components.css` does not yet match a rule below, the rule wins and the component is updated centrally (tracked in `beyond-salt.md`).
../../design-system/RULES.md-184-
../../design-system/RULES.md-185-### 9.1 Buttons
../../design-system/RULES.md-186-| Role | Look | Use for |
../../design-system/RULES.md-187-|---|---|---|
../../design-system/RULES.md-188-| **Primary** | Solid brand blue, white label | The one action that moves the flow forward. One per screen or sheet. |
../../design-system/RULES.md-189-| **Secondary** | White, grey border (`--tm-border-default`), brand label, subtle shadow (`--tm-shadow-button-secondary`) — as SALT | A real alternative action, less likely than the primary. |
../../design-system/RULES.md-190-| **Quiet** | Grey text, no border | Leave, cancel, dismiss, "not now", "back to …". |
../../design-system/RULES.md-191-| **Destructive** | White, red border and label — never solid | Removes or closes something for good (disable, mark unavailable). Never the primary role (Apple HIG). |
../../design-system/RULES.md-192-| **Call end** (special) | Solid red, white label | Only for ending a live call (the phone convention). Nothing else uses it. |
../../design-system/RULES.md-193-
../../design-system/RULES.md-194-- **One height per group** — differ by style, not size (Apple HIG). Full-width action buttons in a pinned bar, sheet or form: **56px, 18 semibold**, whatever their role. Compact inline buttons (e.g. "View Rx" in a content row): **48px, 16 semibold**.
../../design-system/RULES.md-195-- **Icons on buttons (2026-10-24):** primary and secondary buttons carry an icon only when it helps the user recognise the action at a glance — calling, scheduling, viewing, skipping, direction (→ next). No icon when the label must be read: confirming, finalising, releasing, and answers to a question. Quiet buttons never have icons. One icon per button, from `icons.js`, before the label (direction arrows after). **Scope:** labelled buttons only — header icons, the close ×, status and notice icons are not buttons and are not covered; adding time ("Add time" with a plus) counts as scheduling.
../../design-system/RULES.md-196-- **Order, top to bottom:** primary → secondary → quiet. Two secondaries may sit side by side (equal width, label fits on one line at 360px wide with room to spare; otherwise shorten the label or stack). (D-54)
../../design-system/RULES.md-197-- **Icons in buttons:** only when they add meaning (e.g. a phone on "Call patient"). On a side-by-side pair, **both buttons or neither** carry an icon (D-54).
../../design-system/RULES.md-198-- **Labels:** verb first, sentence case, no full stop, never "Click" / "Tap".
../../design-system/RULES.md-199-- **States:** pressed; disabled (design-system disabled style, exempt from contrast); busy (L2). Busy spinner → label gap is 8 on every busy button (A-08, 2026-11-02). A quiet action in progress shows text only ("Ending…"), no spinner. **Busy labels always end with "…"** ("Verifying…", "Sending OTP…") (D-54).
../../design-system/RULES.md-200-- Links inside a sentence stay links (brand colour), not buttons.
../../design-system/RULES.md-201-- **Button icon size steps with the button size** (Apurva, 2026-11-02; replaces the D-81 F27 pair-only rule): **56px action buttons (18px label) → 20px icon; 48px compact buttons (16px label) → 16px icon.** Icons stay on the icon scale (16 / 20 / 24) — like type and spacing, each size is a step on a fixed scale, never an in-between value; the icon is one step at or just above its label (as in Carbon, Atlassian and Fluent). **Icon-only buttons** (Back, Help, notifications, Profile, close ×, viewer controls) are not labelled buttons and keep a **20px** icon. Set centrally in `components.css` by button size (`.tm-btn--lg` → 20, compact → 16, `.tm-btn--icon` → 20), overriding any size in the markup; screens never size button icons. SALT's code copy states no per-button icon size; this is a Truemeds addition (`beyond-salt.md`).
../../design-system/RULES.md-202-
../../design-system/RULES.md-203-### 9.2 Chips and choice grids
../../design-system/RULES.md-204-- **Free-flowing chips** (e.g. frequency, food timing, date): fixed padding and font, width hugs the label, **wrap to the next row** when they don't fit. Never squeeze, clip or shrink text.
../../design-system/RULES.md-205-- **Grid chips** (e.g. dose per time of day, extra doses, time slots): equal-width columns on a 4-column grid. **Every grid on one screen uses the same chip size**; a row with fewer options leaves cells empty (left-aligned) instead of stretching. **A grid starts at its label's left edge**; only a grid with row labels (M / A / N) sits after the label column (D-54). **One chip size per screen:** grids without row labels use the same column width as the M / A / N grid and leave the extra space on the right. Grid chips have 8px side padding — the column sets the size. **Words are free chips, numbers are grid chips:** units (Days / Weeks / Months / Ongoing), frequencies and food timing wrap as free chips; doses, counts and time slots sit in grids (D-54).
../../design-system/RULES.md-206-- Selected = brand tint + brand border (`aria-pressed`). 48px minimum height.
../../design-system/RULES.md-207-
../../design-system/RULES.md-208-### 9.3 Lists, tags and cards
../../design-system/RULES.md-209-- **Rows:** thumb · title · meta · trailing. A **chevron** only when the row opens something. **Row with a status:** title on line 1 (full width); line 2 = one short fact on the left (14/20 semibold, e.g. "Qty 30") and the status tag on the right (`.tm-row__line`, D-54). Details that belong to an edit screen (dose, duration) are not repeated in the row. **Read-only rows** (e.g. a closed task): muted text, no chevron, not tappable, still readable.
../../design-system/RULES.md-210-- **Status tags:** colour by meaning — done = success, needs action = warning, removed / inactive = neutral, failed = critical. **Reserve the tag width** so the row text never re-wraps when the status changes. Tag text meets AA.
../../design-system/RULES.md-211-- **Cards:** one level only, never a card inside a card.
../../design-system/RULES.md-212-- **Status card** (outcome of a task): icon + title (optional one line under it), stays on screen. Not a toast. **Tinted by outcome** (decided D-62, 2026-10-25): `--success` (confirmed, transferred, forwarded — success tint, tick), `--neutral` (pending or no outcome — grey tint, clock / phone-off / info icon), `--warning` (completed with a problem the user must act on — amber tint, warning icon). A plain white status card is not used: the outcome must not look like another content card. **Edge, not shadow** (2026-10-25, option C5): every tone has a 1px edge in its colour (success green-300, neutral grey-200, warning amber-700) and no drop shadow, so it reads as a result, not as a tappable card. Neutral keeps the grey-100 fill.
../../design-system/RULES.md-213-- **Empty state:** `.tm-empty`.
../../design-system/RULES.md-214-
--
ui-screens/app-logic.md:56:## 3. Home and availability `[LOCKED]` (D-36, D-40, D-47, D-53)
ui-screens/app-logic.md-57-- **While Setting… or Adding…** the wheel, the duration chips, Cancel and × are disabled (D-81 F9).
ui-screens/app-logic.md-58-- **Set availability** stays pinned to the bottom of the screen in every state, with or without a notice (D-81 F12, D-43), **inside the action bar** (Round 4, 2026-11-02, item 1). The content above the bar scrolls on short phones (at 360×640 the timer and the wheel are never clipped); the bar never covers the last content; toasts sit above the bar.
ui-screens/app-logic.md-59-- **Time added:** 5:00 + 30 min shows 35:00 (D-81 F10).
ui-screens/app-logic.md-60-- **End availability** is greyed out while offline; the offline notice explains (D-81 F13).
ui-screens/app-logic.md-61-- **Log out confirm:** "Stay signed in" is quiet text, like "Keep available" (D-81 F11, RULES §9.4).
ui-screens/app-logic.md-62-
ui-screens/app-logic.md-63-- Home answers "Am I taking cases right now, and what do I do next?" Nothing is pushed: the doctor **requests** a case (pull model).
ui-screens/app-logic.md-64-- **Set availability:** quick picks 15 / 30 / 45 min, 1 / 2 / 3 hours, plus the wheel (hours and minutes, 15-minute steps). Minimum **15 minutes**, any start time, no maximum (24/7). Confirm starts the countdown.
ui-screens/app-logic.md-65-- **Time remaining:** h:mm:ss from one hour up (1:00:00), m:ss below (9:42). Shows 0:00 when it has ended (D-53, 2026-10-15). The label and the timer do not move when **+ Add time** appears; Add time sits on the value row (A-09). Labels are 14 px grey (A-10).
ui-screens/app-logic.md-66-- **Request a case** while time remains. A request made before the window ends is honoured even if the case arrives after.
ui-screens/app-logic.md-67-- **Add time:** shown when time is running low (near expiry, `[MOCK]` 5 min); same picker in a sheet; "Time added" toast. An error in the add-time sheet sits 16 above its button, as on the page (A-12).
ui-screens/app-logic.md-68-- **End availability:** confirmation sheet. If a request is pending: no new requests, the pending one is honoured, availability ends after it resolves and any assigned case closes ("Ending availability", no time row).
ui-screens/app-logic.md-69-- **Window ends during a case:** the case is never interrupted. The ending card then offers only **Back to Home**; Home shows the ended state.
ui-screens/app-logic.md-70-- **Prescriptions today:** a count only, no earnings. A case counts when its prescription is confirmed. It stays visible after availability ends.
ui-screens/app-logic.md-71-- **Result notices on Home** ("Availability ends soon", setup / add / request failures) sit inside the action bar, above its button (RULES §9.5, A-19). "No cases right now" and offline are the bar's own action, so they sit inside the bar above the button (lane-request 7). Screen-wide standing notices (idle-expired, manually ended, expired-pending, stop-pending) stay at the top of the panel.
ui-screens/app-logic.md-72-- **Checking…** status line in the bar is centred in the button's slot, as on the case page (A-11).
ui-screens/app-logic.md-73-- **No cases:** neutral notice "No cases right now. Try again in a minute." Auto re-check `[OPEN OQ-019]`.
ui-screens/app-logic.md-74-- Notifications bell, Help and Profile icons on Home; the bell never inside a case. Help's content is not designed yet (backlog).
ui-screens/app-logic.md-75-- **Profile page** (D-70: a page, not a sheet — task header with Back, no logo; content ported from the current app with design-system fixes, D-69; full redesign later): doctor name and role · today's earnings (earned, incentive) · User manual · **Faster sign-in on/off** · **Log out** (destructive). During an open case Log out is replaced by "You can log out after this case is closed." Log out is the last item in the content (not pinned). Cards are 16 apart and Log out is 16 below the last card (A-13). The group label "Today's earnings" is 16 semibold, like the other group labels (A-20). Log out asks first in a **sheet**: "Log out? — You'll stop getting cases until you sign in again." · Log out · Stay signed in.
ui-screens/app-logic.md-76-- **Faster sign-in toggle (D-70):** turning it **off** just switches it off (no prompt; OTP from the next sign-in). Turning it **on** opens the phone's prompt, as on the offer screen; if that fails, the toggle stays off and the page shows "Couldn't turn on faster sign-in."; cancelling leaves it off with no message. Hidden if the phone has no screen lock at all (D-64).
ui-screens/app-logic.md-77-- One phone active at a time. Session stays valid through an open case (no OTP over a live case).
ui-screens/app-logic.md-78-
ui-screens/app-logic.md-79-**Source:** approved screens in `ui-screens/home/`; reference behaviour in `ui-screens/home/home-reference.js`.
