ui-screens/app-logic.md-83-## 4. The case journey `[LOCKED]` (project_truth §3–4, D-48–D-56)
ui-screens/app-logic.md-84-
ui-screens/app-logic.md-85-**Stages** (calling stages follow the state table in §5; state IDs in brackets):
ui-screens/app-logic.md-86-
ui-screens/app-logic.md-87-| Stage | What the doctor sees | Bar (top → bottom) | Header Back / phone back |
ui-screens/app-logic.md-88-|---|---|---|---|
ui-screens/app-logic.md-89-| Ready to call (`call.ready`) | Order details + View Rx, medicines, notes (no script card before Call — D-58 pt 18, D-71) | **Call patient** | Header Back → "Leave this case?" sheet: **Release case** / Stay on this case (D-58 pt 20, OQ-024) |
ui-screens/app-logic.md-90-| Calling — the whole call (`call.calling` 2 / 7a, `call.calling-transfer` 11) | End-of-call script in the slot under Order details, above the medicines, from the tap (D-58 pt 18) | Status line "Calling {name}…" (D-74) **only — no Callback on a live call** (CW-A1, D-83). No separate Connecting / On call states (D-58 pt 14). **No End call** — the doctor ends the call on the phone | Header Back hidden from the tap on Call patient / Call again (D-80, D-81 F21); phone back → toast "Finish this case first. Then you can go back to Home." (`a-back-blocked`) |
ui-screens/app-logic.md-91-| Transfer ready (`call.transfer-ready` 12) | Script stays (call still live) | **Confirm & transfer** · Skip HA (full width, under it; no Callback, CW-A1) — shown only once the backend confirms gate time since the patient answered and the call is live (D-58 pt 14) | Blocked |
ui-screens/app-logic.md-92-| Call not valid (`call.ended-early` 6, `call.result-missing` 7d) | No script — the call has ended (D-58 pt 24) | 6: notice · **Call again** · Callback (no Unavailable, D-58 pt 23) · 7d (Cat4): notice · **Confirm prescription** · Callback + Unavailable (reason sheet, D-75) · 7d (Pilot): **Confirm & forward** · Callback + Unavailable, no Skip HA (CW-D2) | Blocked |
ui-screens/app-logic.md-93-| Valid, call ended (`call.valid` 8a / 8b) | No script — the call has ended (D-58 pt 24) | 8a: **Confirm prescription** only · 8b: **Confirm & forward** · ⏭ **Skip HA** full width (only when allowed, §6). No Callback (CW-C3) | Blocked |
ui-screens/app-logic.md-94-| Closed (`completed` / `unavailable`) | Outcome card directly under Order details (where the script was, D-58 point 16); content read-only and muted | **Request next case** · Back to Home (only **Back to Home**, as primary, if availability ended) | Header Back hidden; phone back → Home |
ui-screens/app-logic.md-95-
ui-screens/app-logic.md-96-**Empty case (D-80 pt 4, D-81 F23; D-83 CW-A6, K4):** no **Call patient**. An amber notice at the top of the panel says "No medicines on this order. Our Ops team will check it." (D-84; was "This order has no medicines. Release it — our Ops team will check it.") (where the released case goes is open, OQ-035). The main button is **Release case**, which releases directly (Releasing…, no sheet) and returns the doctor to Home (CW-A5). Header Back does the same. When Order details is hidden, View Rx is left-aligned (B-16).
ui-screens/app-logic.md-97-**Call ended, outcome card (D-81 F26, retired D-83):** the "End the call to get your next case." warning is retired with state 15b; after the hang-up the card is title only, neutral (MAIN-CHECK 2, D-85; `call.forwardedAfterHangup` retired, §14).
ui-screens/app-logic.md-98-**Bar and card rules (Round 4, 2026-11-02):** a bar notice that is the result of an action ("Couldn't confirm…", "Prescribe or disable…") sits inside the action bar above its button (RULES §9.5, A-19). Cards on the case page and Prescribe are 16 apart; the end-of-call script card has 16 padding below in every state (B-03, B-04, B-05). The callback-scheduled card uses the calendar icon and the patient-unavailable card the phone-off icon, the same icons as their buttons (B-22). A two-line patient name makes the header taller, not tighter (B-06). Long medicine titles wrap balanced (B-13).
ui-screens/app-logic.md-99-
ui-screens/app-logic.md-100-**Leaving a case:** the back-blocked toast breaks between its two sentences (B-21). An **attempted call** = leg 2 answered (the patient picked up) (D-58). Once a call is attempted, leaving is blocked until the case is closed (callback, unavailable, confirm). Before that, header **Back** opens the "Leave this case?" sheet — **Release case** (the case returns to the queue) or Stay on this case (D-58 point 20, OQ-024; on Ready and states 3 and 4 only). Header Back is on 1, 3 and 4 only, while the patient has never been reached. It is hidden from the **Call patient** / **Call again** tap, incl. Calling 7a, the 7b question, Transfer, and the callback sheets, and never returns once the patient answered, also on a later 3 / 4 (D-80 pt 1, D-81 F21). Behind the leave sheet, Releasing… and Release failed the screen is **Ready** (D-81 F22). The backend refuses Release once our call request is accepted, unless the result is 3 or 4 (D-80). Release returns the doctor to Home (CW-A5). If the patient answered just before the tap, the backend refuses the release and the doctor stays on the case (`a-release-failed`, "Couldn't release this case. You're still on it."). The unassign action itself is a backend dependency (OQ-024). Help stays available at every stage and is the way to reach Doctor Ops when something keeps failing. App closed or phone off mid-case → reopening goes straight back into the case `[OPEN OQ-025, backend]`.
ui-screens/app-logic.md-101-
ui-screens/app-logic.md-102-**End-of-call script** (D-58 points 18, 21, 24 — copy keys in `messages.json`). Shown from the tap on Call while a call may be live; **hidden once the call has ended** (no one to read it to), except after a failed transfer (15) and B3, where the doctor is still on the line:
ui-screens/app-logic.md-103-- Launch B, Pilot live call (B1, neutral): `call.scriptNeutral` — "I'm writing your prescription now. Our Health Advisor will help you with the next steps."
ui-screens/app-logic.md-104-- Transfer (Pilot, Value Meds, version A — later): `call.scriptTransfer` — "I'm writing your prescription now. Please stay on the line — I'll connect you to our Health Advisor."
ui-screens/app-logic.md-105-- Forward (Pilot, Non-Value Meds, version A — later): `call.scriptForward` — "I'm writing your prescription now. Our Health Advisor will call you to help with the next steps."
ui-screens/app-logic.md-106-- Everything else (Cat4, HA skipped): `call.scriptCat4` — "I'm writing your prescription now. You can track your order in the Truemeds app."
ui-screens/app-logic.md-107-- After a failed transfer / no Health Advisor free: `call.forwardedTell` — "I've written your prescription. Our Health Advisor will call you back to help with the next steps." (one patient script for 15 and B3; the patient is never told about Health Advisor capacity).
