# Run A0 — spec-only acceptance cases

Scope: shell items 1–5c. The latest tester instruction authorizes these artifacts; no app implementation, CSS, screens, private store, or core logic was inspected. The only app source imports are the explicitly allowed synthetic test data and settings. D-97 is the product authority. tm-chotu v0.4.3 (2026-08-25), Rx cadence, was consulted for orientation only; it does not define these project decisions. All dimensions, values, codes and expected results below originate in the cited spec files, rather than live data.

## Definition of done for this delivery

- [auto] Runner parses and "'`--list` imports without app implementation modules.
- [eye] Each scoped requirement has a cited case below, with automation limits explicit.
- [auto] Browser cases use served app/, state URLs, play links and public controls; no store mutation.
- [eye] Only `tests/codex/run-A0/` is written. Main thread reviews adapters and missing evidence before interpreting failures.
- [eye] Passing syntax/inventory does not mean the app passes. App acceptance also requires the manual evidence below and main-thread approval.

Source shorthand: **Brief** = `docs/renders/2026-11-09-build-fast/TERMINAL-BRIEF.md`; **D97** = `docs/context/decision_log.md:987–991`; **Rules** = `../../design-system/RULES.md`; **Logic** = `ui-screens/app-logic.md`; **Data** = `app/data/test-numbers.js`; **Settings** = `app/core/settings.js`; **Contract** = `tests/codex/README.md:29–47` (Driver contract and limits). Ranges identify the exact source passage, not extra scope.

## Cases and evidence required

| ID | Pass condition | Source line | Evidence / automation |
|---|---|---|---|
| A0-layout-* | At 1280×800, 1440×900, 1920×1080, height is clamp(640px, viewport height − 48px, 844px), width is height × 390/844; frame stays centred, exact 390×844 when space allows, otherwise evenly scaled. Geometry tolerance is 2 CSS pixels for border/rounding, not a new design dimension. | Brief:56; D97:988; Rules:119 | auto: all three viewport cases measure enclosing frame around public `#screen`. |
| A0-reference | Reference-page desktop frames also use 390:844; old styles.css remains frozen; recapture every approved picture with D-94 settings and obtain zero differing pixels. No screen or approved picture changes. | Brief:55–56; D97:989 | eye/build evidence: inspect changed-file list, reference frames and complete D-94 comparisons. Deliberately not inferred from app geometry. This tester may not read implementation or write captures elsewhere. |
| A0-layout-* | Exactly one right-hand column, aligned with frame top, no left-gutter Test on phone card; panel does not alter frame size/centring. | Brief:57; Rules:122; D97:988 | auto: row x/y and centred frame; no visible Test on phone label left of frame. eye: verify no unrelated left-gutter control card remains. |
| A0-layout-* | Test on phone is the first folding row, initially open, toggles closed/open; contains QR, instructions, play link and Copy link. | Brief:57–59 | auto: row/default/toggle/QR element/Copy link; network and happy-path tests exercise link. eye: read complete instructions and verify updated happy-path steps rather than failure-path instructions. |
| A0-layout-* | At 1280×800, opening each row (including Story and Call simulator) never pushes another summary off screen; all rows remain in the same ordered column; neither panel nor desktop page scrolls. | Brief:57; Rules:120 | auto: sequential real summary clicks, all summaries bounded by viewport, no ancestor scrolling container or document overflow. eye: expanded row controls also remain usable; summary visibility alone does not prove every expanded control is accessible. |
| A0-network-link | For localhost and 127.0.0.1 with configured network address, QR actually decodes to the advertised non-loopback play host and preserves serving port; Copy link copies that URL and it opens the app. | Brief:58; D97:988 | auto against build'"'s configured server, run once with each loopback base. QR is decoded via BarcodeDetector, never treated as correct merely because an image exists. Missing decoder is a testability failure, not QR failure. |
| A0-network-copy | Exact plain line “Phone and Mac on the same Wi-Fi” appears beneath the QR. Preview-site QR/link uses that site's own origin. | Brief:58 | auto: exact visible line in desktop layout tests. eye: beneath-QR placement, plain styling and preview-origin/QR check on deployed preview; this runner's network case is expressly for local serving. |
| A0-server | scripts/serve.sh runs copy-shared.sh first, serves app/ with python3 -m http.server on port 8080 and prints usable network URL supplied to app. | Brief:58 | eye/build evidence: server launch output and configured local URL. Tester does not read scripts or prescribe an undocumented injection mechanism. |
| A0-happy-path | Untouched default story is Cat4, patient answers, simulated call and record over gate; sign-in → Home → case → prescribe → call → Confirm prescription → Prescription confirmed → Request next case opens next case. Failure options remain selectable. | Brief:59; D97:988 | auto: fresh context, generated play link, real controls, public clock fast-forward, confirmed visible result and next case. eye: Cat4/patient/call/record selected values, failure options and updated QR steps. A1/A2 screens may still be unbuilt at A0: report dependency explicitly, never mask failure or claim end-to-end proof. |
| A0-summaries | Summary text may wrap to two lines; no ellipsis, single-line clamp or horizontally clipped text (including long Turn on / Unlock combinations). | Brief:60; D97:988 | auto: computed overflow/ellipsis checks on default summary descendants. eye: select longest visible combinations; verify actual two-line wrapping, full words, and no more than two lines. Default short summaries alone cannot prove this. |
| A0-inputs-* | Sign-in answers lists each number and code, result in plain words, plus other-valid-number and other-OTP rules; both lists visible on sign-in and OTP, desktop and phone drawer. | Brief:61; Logic:280–295; Data:2–15 | auto: both auth states at desktop and phone/play, visible buttons and result phrases. Phone drawer opener is a role/name adapter. |
| A0-inputs-* | Tap each listed sign-in number fills running sign-in field; tap each listed code fills running OTP field. No auto-submit is required by spec. | Brief:61; Data:2–13 | auto: every data entry in matching screen, desktop and phone drawer; exact field inputValue. |
| A0-data-origin | Display list comes from same test-numbers.js data as mock server rather than duplicate hardcoding. | Brief:61 | eye/build review: shared data provenance. Matching visible content is necessary but cannot prove implementation provenance. No implementation read by tester. |
| A0-settings | Row renamed Timings and limits; values have plain names (Valid-call minimum, OTP lock, Resend waits), units seconds/minutes for time, source-derived Rule / Stand-in tag and reference on hover or tap. | Brief:62; D97:988; Settings:1–4,10–47,59–62 | auto: compares every exported setting value/source/ref, checks example names, no old Settings row; title-hover adapter. eye: all remaining labels genuinely plain, references usable on touch, no spurious units on counts/currency. |
| A0-order | Test on phone · Story · Jump to a state · Sign-in answers · Home and case answers · Call simulator · quiet Advanced label · Timings and limits · Event log at bottom. | Brief:62 | auto: summary order/position, Advanced between call and timings. eye: quiet styling and no extra rows below Event log. |
| A0-shell-contract | Frame rounded, overflow hidden, transform anchoring; one internal content scroll region, pinned header, overlays inside frame; below desktop breakpoint app fills screen with viewport overlays. | Rules:118–123 | eye: existing layout_check and overlay/mobile behavior evidence. Not proven by summary geometry; A0 must retain these standing §7 constraints. |

### Exact test-data oracle

From Logic:284–293 and Data:2–15: "'`9000000001` → Not registered/sign-up; `9000000002` → Account inactive/Call Doctor Ops; `9000000003` → Too many attempts/countdown; `9000000004` → Couldn'"'t send; "'`9000000005` → Number locked. `1234` → Correct/signs in; `0000` → Code expired; `9999` → Couldn'"'t verify/server error. Other valid mobile → Code sent/OTP; other OTP → Wrong code, tries count down, fifth locks. These are synthetic inputs, not personal data. This suite tests panel display and tap-fill; entry-journeys owns full authentication outcomes.

### Source ambiguity to report, not silently resolve

Settings:38–43 has "'`source: "review tool"`, whereas Brief:62 permits Rule / Stand-in tags only. Runner provisionally maps every non-rule source to Stand-in, including review tool. Main thread must confirm this adapter/classification. Counts and earnings also exist in Settings:20–47; time units apply only to `time: true`, counts remain counts and earnings remain currency. Reference title attributes are a test adapter choice, not a UI requirement: if references open on tap instead, adapt to that public action without requiring titles in product.

## Running and driver limits

```sh
node tests/codex/run-A0/all.mjs --list
CHROME='"'/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome' node tests/codex/run-A0/all.mjs
CODEX_FILTER=A0-network CODEX_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080/ A0_NETWORK_HOST=192.168.1.20 CHROME='/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome' node tests/codex/run-A0/all.mjs
"'```

The host above is an illustrative configuration placeholder, not a measured network address. Configure the actual build server first; this tester does not invent server configuration endpoints. Repeat network case with `http://127.0.0.1:8080/`. With no base URL runner serves app/ read-only on an ephemeral loopback port; no app code is inspected to derive expectations. External server should serve app/ at supplied base; include trailing slash. Fresh browser storage per case. Failures exit nonzero; no skipped/expected-failure cases. No reports/screenshots/dependencies are written.

Public `#screen`, `#rp-link`, `#tm-login-mobile`, `#c`, `#medicines-list` and `window.__tm.clock.fastForward` follow entry-journeys/Contract. Details/summary follows folding-row semantics. Test-list buttons, drawer opener name matching Review/Demo/Controls, reference titles, frame-ancestor inference, Home availability button sequence and pending-medicine clicks are **unverified public UI adapters**, not additional product decisions. If markup exposes equivalent roles or reference popovers, report and correct adapter only, preserving expected behavior. Happy-path fast-forward waits on visible Confirm rather than mutating story; it intentionally does not force outcomes. No private state reads/writes or screen/core imports.

Validation performed for this delivery: node syntax check and complete inventory import. Browser execution not performed; no claim that current app passes. Build thread records each executable ID and each eye case as pass/fail with evidence, resolves adapter discrepancies against Contract, and supplies manual acceptance evidence. Brief:63 existing checks, before/after screenshots and publishing are build-owner tasks outside this tester'"'s write scope.
